{"chapter": "spaces-groupoids", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "06P5", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-properties-group-spaces}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e70e7f07d0ee39d16673130677695290cc3c815adc1a5243fc8a679c4ac6f231", "source_text": "Properties of group algebraic spaces", "source_text_hash": "sha256:53766e97e74ddda11fb4793efb2bdcea6bb081457490ab6654746bddea145649", "unit_id": "tag:06P5:title"}
{"chapter": "spaces-groupoids", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06P5", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a01317e3093845b6569e787a068042cf76d5d7b2131b962501e8f163cbacada2", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this section we collect some simple properties of group algebraic spaces\nwhich hold over any base.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d2f553cf902a63a13051c59a9a1db19306029eaddefc8dc440900ae8fc4ef06f", "unit_id": "tag:06P5:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "spaces-groupoids", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06P5", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$B$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$G$", "MATH_0005": "$B$", "MATH_0006": "$G \\to B$", "MATH_0007": "$e : B \\to G$", "SPACE_0001": "\\ ", "SPACE_0002": "\\ ", "SPACE_0003": "\\ ", "SPACE_0004": "\\ "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-group-scheme-separated}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:cd8f5383cd218a29980fd75366419783ac7179de4ea18aefb772fd1e748f115e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d9246b6a3e6e47f1d32b97979b3b25e7246728a2edff7edb9f3bed1dda543a18", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be an algebraic space over <MATH_0003>.\nLet <MATH_0004> be a group algebraic space over <MATH_0005>.\nThen <MATH_0006> is separated (resp.<SPACE_0001>quasi-separated, resp.<SPACE_0002>locally separated)\nif and only if the identity morphism <MATH_0007> is a closed immersion\n(resp.<SPACE_0003>quasi-compact, resp.<SPACE_0004>an immersion).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:95dd268b72e0f8f074b43c31de085fcbe83372fbdf950c93e9baff96fcce3601", "unit_id": "tag:06P6:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces-groupoids", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06P5", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$e$", "MATH_0002": "$G \\to B$", "MATH_0003": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nG \\ar[r]_-{\\Delta_{G/B}} \\ar[d] &\nG \\times_B G \\ar[d]^{(g, g') \\mapsto m(i(g), g')} \\\\\nB \\ar[r]^e & G\n}\n$$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Delta_{G/B}$", "MATH_0005": "$e$", "MATH_0006": "$e$", "MATH_0007": "$\\Delta_{G/B}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-section-immersion}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{spaces-lemma-base-change-immersions}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-base-change-quasi-compact}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{spaces-lemma-base-change-immersions}", "SPACE_0001": "\\ ", "SPACE_0002": "\\ ", "SPACE_0003": "\\ ", "SPACE_0004": "\\ ", "SPACE_0005": "\\ ", "SPACE_0006": "\\ ", "SPACE_0007": "\\ ", "SPACE_0008": "\\ "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:80d3cc2c254ba49238113dd62996559999fb08d3624342834981aec8b5f79959", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a0f96e8ca09b47d189ec4efc11e82727aa8361fd958e6953aa76aff6a25611ab", "source_text": "We recall that by\nMorphisms of Spaces, Lemma <REF_0001>\nwe have that <MATH_0001> is a closed immersion (resp.<SPACE_0001>quasi-compact, resp.<SPACE_0002>an\nimmersion) if <MATH_0002> is separated (resp.<SPACE_0003>quasi-separated, resp.<SPACE_0004>locally\nseparated).\nFor the converse, consider the diagram\n<MATH_0003>\nIt is an exercise in the functorial point of view in algebraic geometry\nto show that this diagram is cartesian. In other words, we see that\n<MATH_0004> is a base change of <MATH_0005>. Hence if <MATH_0006> is a\nclosed immersion (resp.<SPACE_0005>quasi-compact, resp.<SPACE_0006>an immersion) so is\n<MATH_0007>, see\nSpaces, Lemma <REF_0002>\n(resp.<SPACE_0007>Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma\n<REF_0003>,\nresp.<SPACE_0008>Spaces, Lemma <REF_0004>).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4245a46cf32f62d81f75b0ec64dc1dad918ca5ab0b491d9f485080d1303478b7", "unit_id": "tag:06P6:proof"}
{"chapter": "spaces-groupoids", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06P5", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$B$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$G$", "MATH_0005": "$B$", "MATH_0006": "$G \\to B$", "MATH_0007": "$G \\to B$", "MATH_0008": "$G \\to B$", "MATH_0009": "$e(b)$", "MATH_0010": "$b \\in |B|$", "SPACE_0001": "\\ ", "SPACE_0002": "\\ "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-group-scheme-unramified-or-lqf}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e772140a89b66155f12ce992cc7092f16ba12d66a00433ff6a9961d4938fd263", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d6faddc5f5d04b27fcea003b3118c27edb89d4c13170e44f90c69c32ed68b695", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be an algebraic space over <MATH_0003>.\nLet <MATH_0004> be a group algebraic space over <MATH_0005>. Assume <MATH_0006>\nis locally of finite type. Then\n<MATH_0007> is unramified (resp.<SPACE_0001>locally quasi-finite)\nif and only if <MATH_0008> is unramified (resp.<SPACE_0002>quasi-finite)\nat <MATH_0009> for all <MATH_0010>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d8ce8120e7990cf9f0f30ee95511ae29f5d1190bc5dcbba7fc3593cfc713ca8c", "unit_id": "tag:0DSI:statement"}
